      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding on to this as I've come to understand more about avatar scaling, there really needs to be a way to prevent a world author from scaling you without your consent (perhaps a toggle in the quick menu for \"allow world author to scale you\" which you could turn off. I would not feel comfortable going to  a world and then having my height changed without my consent by the world author, for the same reasons outlined in the original post. My body is my body and no one should be doing anything to me without my consent.\n\nI understand that some people may not understand this, but to many people in vrchat our avatars are the same as our irl bodies (or even more our bodies than the irl ones). And consent needs to be asked, always. \n\nIf a world really wanted to be able to scale people, they could put like a sign near spawn explaining why to people and ask them to turn the function on. But they should always be asking to do that, not telling me that something will be done to me no matter how i feel.\n\nI would still want to be able to scale myself even if i have disabled the world author's ability to scale me. Otherwise i will not be able to use scaling at all just because i have personal boundaries and care about consent, which goes against the point of having scaling.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-06-23T00:25:22.502Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In every world, allow scaling between a smaller range of \"average\" eye heights  - perhaps between 2-9 ft tall. This height range allows players to match the height of the most common avatar scales, and will already have been accounted for by every world creator. Make this always persist between worlds. This is important for users to feel safe and to not be scaled suddenly without their consent.\n\nCommon avatar height categories this would cover:\n\n2 ft-4 ft: Kon and small furries\n\n3-5 feet: many japanese avatar styles\n\n4-8 feet: western human avatars\n\n6-9 feet: tall furries\n\nAll these sizes are very reasonable to be in and are not disruptive or immersion-breaking in any way. Different social groups have a different average height, which it is important to be close to for normal interaction. This would allow people to use one avatar for different friend groups. If this isn't implemented, I will personally have to upload 5 avatar sizes for every avatar I make, in order to be able to interact with all my friends.\n\nBeing forced to change size suddenly on world change is very disruptive, and goes against VRChat's policy of having users be able to choose their own options in order to have an experience where they feel safe and in control.\n\nAs an example, I have one avatar uploaded. It has an eye height of 3 feet, because many of my friends are short and I want to be at eye height with them to interact normally. I hang out with that friend group, and then leave to spend time with my other friend. He has an eye height of probably 9 or 10 feet. I want to be similar height with him, so I scale myself to  have an eye height of 8 feet. We go world hopping, and I am having fun. Then we enter a world with scaling turned off. Suddenly I am the size of my friend's foot. I feel upset and maybe a bit scared. Perhaps I was not in a safe brain space to be small, especially suddenly and without my consent. When I log off, I immediately go and upload 5 avatar versions of my avatar, each with a different scale, to avoid having such a bad experience again.\n\nSimilarly, if I upload a tall avatar and scale myself down to spend time with small friends, I am in danger on world change of stepping on them or having a social dynamic I do not want.",
